From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rust: build LLVM through ccache when the build uses it

With CONFIG_CCACHE, the build's C and C++ go through ccache, but
rust/host's LLVM, most of its build time, did not: a host toolchain
built again, as after a change of its flags, compiled all of LLVM
again. Give rustbuild the build's ccache (build.ccache).

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 lang/rust/Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/lang/rust/Makefile b/lang/rust/Makefile
index d054045..57aba99 100644
--- a/lang/rust/Makefile
+++ b/lang/rust/Makefile
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@ HOST_CONFIGURE_ARGS = \
 	--enable-cargo-native-static \
 	--bootstrap-cache-path=$(DL_DIR)/rustc \
 	--set=llvm.download-ci-llvm=false \
+	$(if $(CONFIG_CCACHE),--set=build.ccache=$(STAGING_DIR_HOST)/bin/ccache) \
 	$(TARGET_CONFIGURE_ARGS)
 
 define Host/Uninstall
